// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`documents Full Access as a create-only choice with a Settings default 1`] = `
"Usage: opencove node create agent [--near <selector> | --root-canvas | --space <id> | <other-target-space-options>] [options]

Create an agent node

Agent-terminal prompt rules:
- Launches: describe a task in a sentence; single tokens and provider command names are refused.
- Provider controls: no leading /; Claude also refuses ! # &; Codex, OpenCode, Pi and Gemini also refuse !.
- Exit aliases: no exit, quit, :q, :q!, :wq or :wq!.
- File references: no @ anywhere. Read approved content with opencove fs read --uri file:///workspace/README.md --fields content (replace the absolute URI), then paste the content.
- Codex skills: no $name or linked skill mentions; paste the instructions.
- Leading dashes: Claude Code and Pi launches refuse prompts starting with -.
- Null characters: remove NUL from the prompt.

Use --prompt or --prompt-file with --wait to wait for the initial Claude Code or Codex turn. Add --read for its exact reply; unavailable replies return reply: null with replyUnavailableReason. Check outcome: every ended outcome exits 0. Waiting for the user exits 10, an exited target 11, timeout 124 and interruption 130. Unsupported providers refuse after creation; the node remains.

--timeout covers first-turn identification and waiting (default 20s; minimum 250ms); creation keeps its own 20s budget. If no first turn is observed, lifecycle telemetry may be unavailable even if the agent is running or has finished. Inspect the existing session; do not recreate the node or resend the prompt. Errors keep known nodeId, sessionId and turnId. Never repeat creation after an error: resume agent wait/read with those IDs. With --wait, -q prints only the node ID after completion. Stderr shows "Created agent node <nodeId> (session <sessionId>)." before identification, then "Waiting for turn <turnId> of node <nodeId>..." with an interruption-only continuation command. The final JSON and exit status report the result.

For agents creating helper nodes, recommend --near @self to place them near the caller in its current Space (or root). --near is opt-in; combine with --root-canvas to place outside Spaces. It cannot be combined with --frame.

Without explicit x/y, root-canvas placement searches next to you when run inside OpenCove and avoids Spaces. If your node belongs to another project, the search starts at the canvas origin. Use --focus to reveal the node. A --frame with both x and y places the node exactly there, even if it overlaps a Space.

Default target inside OpenCove: your current Space, or the root canvas when you are outside any Space. An explicit --project alone does not select a container; creation also needs --near, --root-canvas or a Space target.

Target container (choose one):
  --root-canvas                                 Create on the project's root canvas, outside every Space
  --space <id>                                  Select a space by its ID; also accepts @self, an exact name or a unique ID prefix (6+ characters)
  --space-name <name> [--project <id>]          Find a named space, optionally within a project
  --worker <id-or-name> --branch <branch>       Find a space by worker and Git branch
  --worker <id-or-name> --path <absolute-path>  Find a space by worker and working directory
  --project <id>                                Select the root-canvas project, or narrow a Space lookup; also accepts @self, an exact name or a unique ID prefix (6+ characters)

Options:
  --prompt <text>             Set the initial agent prompt
  --prompt-file <path|->      Read prompt from a UTF-8 file, or use - for stdin
  --wait                      Wait for the initial prompt turn to end
  --read                      Include the exact initial turn reply; requires --wait
  --timeout <duration>        First-turn identification and wait budget (default 20s; minimum 250ms)
  --provider <id>             Select the agent provider. Accepted IDs: claude-code, codex, opencode, gemini, pi, kimi; omit to use the configured default
  --model <id>                Select the agent model
  --task <nodeId>             Link to an existing task in the same Space and move it to doing
  --full-access <true|false>  Set Full Access for this agent and its restarts; omit to follow Settings
  --title <text>              Set a fixed window name; omit on creation to keep automatic titles
  --frame <json>              Set x, y, width and height as a JSON object; appliedFrame and frameAdjusted report any changes
  --near <selector>           Place near a reference node; recommend --near @self for helper nodes; also accepts @self, @parent, an exact name or a unique ID prefix (6+ characters)
  --focus                     Focus after creation
  -q, --quiet                 Print only the created object identifier followed by a newline

Table output (-o table): not supported.
Projectable fields: id, kind, title, projectId, spaceId, frame, frame.x, frame.y, frame.width, frame.height, status, sessionId, spawnedBy, lineageDepth, lineageStatus, data, data.kind, turnId, outcome, endedAt, reply, reply.nodeId, reply.sessionId, reply.turnId, reply.deliveryIds, reply.promptIds, reply.promptId, reply.outcome, reply.message, reply.truncated, reply.messageKind, reply.persisted, reply.memoryOnlyReason, reply.source, replyUnavailableReason, data.provider, data.prompt, data.model, data.effectiveModel, data.executionDirectory, data.expectedDirectory, data.taskId

Field descriptions:
  spawnedBy      ID of the node that created this node; null for a root or unavailable lineage
  lineageDepth   A node started by the user has lineageDepth 1; each agent-created generation adds one. Null when lineage is unavailable
  lineageStatus  recorded when creation is recorded, root when no parent is recorded, unavailable when lineage cannot be read

Projection example:
  opencove node create agent --space space-123 --fields id,title
  {"revision":1,"projectId":"p","spaceId":"space-123","node":{"id":"n","title":"Agent"}}

Examples:
  opencove node create agent --space space-123 --prompt "Review the test failures" --wait --read --timeout 2m
  opencove node create agent --root-canvas --project project-123 --title "Release review" --pretty

Global options: see "opencove --help".
"
`;
